
@startuml class
title CampusEats - Class Diagram
left to right direction

class User {
  +id: Integer
  +name: String
  +email: String
  +password_hash: String
  +role: String
  +set_password(password)
  +check_password(password): Boolean
}

class FoodListing {
  +id: Integer
  +vendor_id: Integer
  +title: String
  +description: Text
  +portions: Integer
  +portions_remaining: Integer
  +cancelled: Boolean
  +pickup_location: String
  +dietary_tags: String
  +pickup_start: DateTime
  +pickup_end: DateTime
  +created_at: DateTime
  --
  +available(): Query
  +portions_reserved: Integer
  +status: String
}

class Reservation {
  +id: Integer
  +listing_id: Integer
  +student_id: Integer
  +portions: Integer
  +pickup_code: String
  +status: String
}

User "1" -- "0..*" FoodListing : creates (vendor)
User "1" -- "0..*" Reservation : places (student)
FoodListing "1" -- "0..*" Reservation : receives

note right of User
  US1: role = student or vendor.
  Passwords are stored as bcrypt hashes.
end note

note bottom of FoodListing
  US2, US3, US5 implementation.

  dietary_tags is stored as a String.
  portions_remaining tracks available portions.
  cancelled indicates listing cancellation.
  created_at records listing creation time.

  available() filters available listings.
  status and portions_reserved are
  calculated properties.
end note

note bottom of Reservation
  US4, US6, US7 implementation.

  Reservations belong to a student
  and a food listing.

  status tracks reservation state.
  pickup_code is a unique 6-digit code.
end note

@enduml
